Extending transfer learning to cooperative multi-agent reinforcement learning (MARL) has recently attracted considerable attention. Nevertheless, most existing methods rely on a single shared policy, which restricts the diversity of transferred policies and limits the exploration of the policy space. To overcome this limitation, we propose a new framework allowing agents to retain multiple policies. In this setup, each policy is trained independently and subsequently pruned based on its performance. We show that our approach is effective for both single-source and multi-source transfer learning scenarios. Furthermore, extensive experiments on cooperative MARL tasks indicate that our method significantly surpasses existing techniques in both single-source and multi-source contexts. The source code can be found at https://github.com/ChenYuan1999/MultiPolicyTransfer.
